IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa24-officers`
IMPORT `coa24-penalty`

-- coa24-false-statements.l4: Part 35, ss 1112 to 1112B of the Companies Act 2006: false statements to the registrar: the
-- basic offence, the aggravated offence and the national security defence (lines 15978-16010 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST TRUE is the text
-- saying yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`); NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why,
-- as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). The offences are "limited by their own wording" ("without reasonable excuse",
-- "knowingly", "in a material particular"): where an element is missing the answer is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE
-- (marginal reading (b) for a lawyer in NOTES.md).

§ `Part 35: false statements (ss 1112 to 1112B)`

-- ---- s 1112 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15979 | (1) It is an offence for a person, without reasonable excuse, to—
-- src:15980 | (a) deliver or cause to be delivered to the registrar, for any purpose of the Companies Acts, a document that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, or
-- src:15981 | (b) make to the registrar, for any purpose of the Companies Acts, a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
@ref s 1112(1) The basic offence: delivering a false document or making a false statement without reasonable excuse (src:15979-15981)
GIVEN `the person delivered or caused to be delivered to the registrar, for a purpose of the Companies Acts, a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made to the registrar, for a purpose of the Companies Acts, a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112(1) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF       (`the person delivered or caused to be delivered to the registrar, for a purpose of the Companies Acts, a document` OR `the person made to the registrar, for a purpose of the Companies Acts, a statement`)
         AND `the document or statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
         AND (NOT `the person has a reasonable excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person, without reasonable excuse, to— (a) deliver or cause to be delivered to the registrar, for any purpose of the Companies Acts, a document that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, or (b) make to the registrar, for any purpose of the Companies Acts, a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular"

-- src:15982 | (2) Where the offence is committed by a firm, every officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence.
@ref s 1112(2) Where the offence is committed by a firm every officer in default also commits it (src:15982)
GIVEN `the offence was committed by` IS A `Kind of person`
      `s 1112(1) the offence was committed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      position IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person`
      conduct IS A `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112(2) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `the offence was committed by`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1112(1) the offence was committed`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 1121 the person is an officer in default` position conduct
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the offence is committed by a firm" and the offence of subsection (1) is not made out on the facts given
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the offence is committed by a firm"

-- src:15983 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:15984 | (a) on summary conviction in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:15985 | (b) on summary conviction in Scotland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale;
-- src:15986 | (c) on summary conviction in Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1112(3) The punishment on summary conviction (src:15983-15986)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 1112(3) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHEN Scotland THEN Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- ---- s 1112A ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15988 | (1) It is an offence for a person knowingly to—
-- src:15989 | (a) deliver or cause to be delivered to the registrar, for any purpose of the Companies Acts, a document that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, or
-- src:15990 | (b) make to the registrar, for any purpose of the Companies Acts, a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
@ref s 1112A(1) The aggravated offence: knowingly delivering a false document or making a false statement (src:15988-15990)
GIVEN `the person delivered or caused to be delivered to the registrar, for a purpose of the Companies Acts, a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made to the registrar, for a purpose of the Companies Acts, a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112A(1) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF       (`the person delivered or caused to be delivered to the registrar, for a purpose of the Companies Acts, a document` OR `the person made to the registrar, for a purpose of the Companies Acts, a statement`)
         AND `the document or statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
         AND `the person acted knowingly`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person knowingly to— (a) deliver or cause to be delivered to the registrar, for any purpose of the Companies Acts, a document that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, or (b) make to the registrar, for any purpose of the Companies Acts, a statement that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular"

-- src:15991 | (2) Where the offence is committed by a firm, every officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence.
@ref s 1112A(2) Where the offence is committed by a firm every officer in default also commits it (src:15991)
GIVEN `the offence was committed by` IS A `Kind of person`
      `s 1112A(1) the offence was committed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      position IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person`
      conduct IS A `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112A(2) the officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` `the offence was committed by`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1112A(1) the offence was committed`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 1121 the person is an officer in default` position conduct
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the offence is committed by a firm" and the offence of subsection (1) is not made out on the facts given
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the offence is committed by a firm"

-- (3): the imprisonment on summary conviction in England and Wales is "the general limit in a magistrates' court", which the
-- Act does not state: it comes in as an input, and s 1131(2) substitutes six months for an offence committed before 2 May 2022.
-- src:15992 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:15993 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:15994 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:15995 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or a fine (or both);
-- src:15996 | (ii) in Scotland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:15997 | (iii) in Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 1112A(3) The punishment (src:15992-15997)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court` IS A MAYBE Period
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1112A(3) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 2, Years)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) divides summary conviction into England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1131(2) the term of imprisonment the provision refers to` `date the offence was committed` `the general limit in a magistrates' court`
        WHEN JUST term THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST term
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the general limit in a magistrates’ court" is not stated in the Act
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 12, Months)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)

-- ---- s 1112B ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15999 | (1) A person to whom a certificate is issued by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this section is not liable for the commission of any offence relating to the delivery to the registrar, or the making of a statement, that is misleading, false or deceptive.
@ref s 1112B(1) A person to whom a certificate is issued is not liable (src:15999)
GIVEN `a certificate is issued to the person by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence relates to the delivery to the registrar, or the making of a statement, that is misleading, false or deceptive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112B(1) the person is liable for the commission of the offence` MEANS
    IF `a certificate is issued to the person by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this section` AND `the offence relates to the delivery to the registrar, or the making of a statement, that is misleading, false or deceptive`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person to whom a certificate is issued by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this section is not liable for the commission of any offence relating to the delivery to the registrar, or the making of a statement, that is misleading, false or deceptive"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a person to whom a certificate is issued and an offence relating to a false delivery or statement

-- src:16000 | (2) The Secretary of State may issue a certificate to a person for the purposes of this section only if satisfied that it is necessary for the person to engage in conduct amounting to such an offence—
-- src:16001 | (a) in the interests of national security, or
-- src:16002 | (b) for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime.
@ref s 1112B(2) The Secretary of State may issue a certificate only if satisfied that it is necessary (src:16000-16002)
GIVEN `satisfied that it is necessary for the person to engage in conduct amounting to such an offence in the interests of national security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `satisfied that it is necessary for the person to engage in conduct amounting to such an offence for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112B(2) the Secretary of State may issue the certificate` MEANS
    IF `satisfied that it is necessary for the person to engage in conduct amounting to such an offence in the interests of national security` OR `satisfied that it is necessary for the person to engage in conduct amounting to such an offence for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State may issue a certificate to a person for the purposes of this section only if satisfied that it is necessary for the person to engage in conduct amounting to such an offence— (a) in the interests of national security, or (b) for the purposes of preventing or detecting serious crime"

-- src:16003 | (3) A certificate under this section may be revoked by the Secretary of State at any time.
@ref s 1112B(3) A certificate may be revoked at any time (src:16003)
GIVEN `a certificate has been issued under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112B(3) the Secretary of State may revoke the certificate` MEANS
    IF `a certificate has been issued under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate under this section may be revoked by the Secretary of State at any time"

-- src:16004 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2)(b)—
-- src:16005 | (a) “crime” means conduct which—
-- src:16006 | (i) constitutes a criminal offence, or
-- src:16007 | (ii) is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence, and
-- src:16008 | (b) crime is “serious” if—
-- src:16009 | (i) the offence which is or would be constituted by the conduct is an offence for which the maximum sentence (in any part of the United Kingdom) is imprisonment for 3 years or more, or
-- src:16010 | (ii) the conduct involves the use of violence, results in substantial financial gain or is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose.
@ref s 1112B(4)(a) Definitions for subsection (2)(b): "crime" (src:16004-16010)
GIVEN `the conduct constitutes a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112B(4)(a) the conduct is crime` MEANS
    IF `the conduct constitutes a criminal offence` OR `the conduct is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“crime” means conduct which— (i) constitutes a criminal offence, or (ii) is, or corresponds to, any conduct which, if it all took place in any one part of the United Kingdom, would constitute a criminal offence"

@ref s 1112B(4)(b) crime is "serious" (src:16008-16010)
GIVEN `the maximum sentence for the offence in any part of the United Kingdom, in years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
      `the conduct involves the use of violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct results in substantial financial gain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1112B(4)(b) the crime is serious` MEANS
    IF       `the maximum sentence for the offence in any part of the United Kingdom, in years of imprisonment` AT LEAST 3
          OR `the conduct involves the use of violence`
          OR `the conduct results in substantial financial gain`
          OR `the conduct is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "crime is “serious” if— (i) the offence which is or would be constituted by the conduct is an offence for which the maximum sentence (in any part of the United Kingdom) is imprisonment for 3 years or more, or (ii) the conduct involves the use of violence, results in substantial financial gain or is conduct by a large number of persons in pursuit of a common purpose"
